SKEW — 10-bit frame, S at bit 5

  Check reads bit 0 as F and bit 5 as S.  At skew d it reads
  bit d as F and bit (d+5) mod 10 as S.

   skew    as F    as S  what
      0       F       S  true alignment
      1      C0      C4  payload pair, five apart (C0,C4)
      2      C1      C5  payload pair, five apart (C1,C5)
      3      C2      C6  payload pair, five apart (C2,C6)
      4      C3      C7  payload pair, five apart (C3,C7)
      5       S       F  header on itself
      6      C4      C0  payload pair, five apart (C4,C0)
      7      C5      C1  payload pair, five apart (C5,C1)
      8      C6      C2  payload pair, five apart (C6,C2)
      9      C7      C3  payload pair, five apart (C7,C3)

  Payload pairs five apart: (C0,C4) (C1,C5) (C2,C6) (C3,C7).
  Four unkeyable pairs at an exchange (cf. one on 16-bit).

GUARD — 10-bit frame, 16-state SF, pads on S

  Default candidate 0,8 = 0,1 (same parity as mf8_16).  Half of ten
  is odd, so 0,5 = 0,1 is the dead analogue (period-2 satisfies it).

  layout                                 F word every  one data, worst   idle every  voice 4-run
  0,8 = 0,1  (family)                        0 / 2560         0 / 2560     0 / 2560     1 in 337
  0,5 = 0,1  (half of ten)                   0 / 2560      2304 / 2560     0 / 2560     1 in 627
  0,6 = 0,1  (mf8_10 lean)                   0 / 2560         0 / 2560     0 / 2560     1 in 432
  0,8 = 1,1  (F-word hole)                2304 / 2560      1024 / 2560     0 / 2560     1 in 427

  Prefer 0,8 = 0,1 if clean: same decode as 16-bit, free octet counter.

SLOT RULES — 10-bit × 16-SF, S at 5, word 0xFFFE, guard 0,8

